 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? That's because dry acrylic paint gets thinner, and the thinner it is, the darker it looks. There are two ways to fix it. You can use a thin layer of clear varnish, or you can sand it down and paint fresh top coat. Yes, dip a thin sheet of paper into the dry painting, and see how dark it gets. If it's dark, varnish it. Then redo the top coat, or use glitter paint instead. It gives the gloss without the thinning.",
